%I A400801 #11 Oct 20 2026 13:25:17
%S A400801 18,50,54,75,90,98,126,147,150,162,198,234,242,245,250,270,294,306,
%T A400801 338,342,350,363,375,378,414,450,486,490,507,522,525,550,558,578,594,
%U A400801 605,630,650,666,686,702,722,726,735,738,750,774,810,825,845,846,847,850,867,882,918,950,954,975,990
%N A400801 Nonsquarefree numbers that are not divisible by the square of their least prime factor.
%C A400801 As this sequence is the complement within A013929 (the nonsquarefree numbers) of A283050 (numbers divisible by the square of their least prime factor) it has asymptotic density 0.06197486275595... = A229099 - A283071.
%H A400801 Michael De Vlieger, <a href="/A400801/b400801.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%t A400801 s = Select[Range[1000], Not @* SquareFreeQ]; Select[s, ! Divisible[#, FactorInteger[#][[1, 1]]^2] &] (* _Michael De Vlieger_, Oct 11 2026 *)
%t A400801 (* Alternative: *)
%t A400801 Select[Range[1000],!SquareFreeQ[#]&&Mod[#,FactorInteger[#][[1,1]]^2]!=0&] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Oct 20 2026 *)
%Y A400801 Intersection of A247180 and A375397.
%Y A400801 Subsequence of A071365, A332785.
%Y A400801 Subsequences include A258211 (even terms), A398442, A398802, A398864, A398948.
%Y A400801 See the comments for the relationships with A013929, A229099, A283050, A283071.
%K A400801 nonn,easy,new
%O A400801 1,1
